# Line endings are LF on every system, whatever git's local setting says.
#
# Measured on 2026-09-29, first run of the Windows matrix: Git for Windows checks text files
# out with CRLF by default, and `node src/readme.ts --check` then read a README whose
# nineteen multi-line figure blocks no longer matched what the generator produces (the
# single-line blocks matched, which is the signature). The gallery cache key moved for the
# same reason: it hashes the sources it depends on, and the sources had grown a carriage
# return per line. Nothing in the repository had changed; the checkout had.
#
# `text=auto` lets git tell text from binary; `eol=lf` fixes the working-tree ending. The
# index already held every text file as LF (git ls-files --eol: 285 lf, 4 binary), so this
# file changes no committed byte; it stops a checkout from changing them.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.gif binary
